{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0175mrZSnWScgHa5xnSn5K3X","type":"tool_result","content":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--rewritten-forms-rerun/results.csv rows=11 PASS=8 FAIL=2\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--signed-in-live/results.csv rows=16 PASS=10 FAIL=5\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--probe-guard-fix/results.csv rows=3 PASS=2 FAIL=0\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-11-21--two-stage-replay--compiled/results.csv rows=6 PASS=6 FAIL=0\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--clickup-real-browser/results.csv rows=6 PASS=4 FAIL=1\n\n23:- The work needs stealth on a signed-in site, and the operator has authorized it under R-SEC-2\n33:- Evading CAPTCHAs, anti-bot walls or access controls against a site's terms (R-SEC-2 forbids it)\n61:- **Neither works:** report the install command and hand the decision to the operator. Never install implicitly (R-SEC-3).\n112:**R-SEC-1 signed-in profiles.** \"Default to the Bladebro-owned agent-browser profile; use `BLADE_HOME`/`BLADE_FRESH=1` for task isolation. Any real-browser (`rb`) lane requires an explicit operator request, and the operator must select the profile/account before control is handed over. Use `attach` whenever the browser must remain caller-owned and open; do not use `profile` on a live branded Chrome. Gate mutations behind `rb pause`/`rb resume` and keep consent-sensitive actions human-in-the-loop. Never pass `--account` to `aside mcp` or `aside repl`, and keep a single-writer lock per account/profile. Re-capture detection output each session and redact cookie/credential values.\"\n114:**R-SEC-2 stealth and site terms of service.** \"Treat stealth as operator-authorized only. Before enabling a real-browser lane on a target site, the operator must confirm the site's terms of service and access rules; do not use Bladebro to evade CAPTCHAs, anti-bot walls, or access controls where doing so breaches those terms or applicable law. A `blocked:` verdict is terminal — report it and stop; do not re-issue the action, swap fingerprints, or otherwise route around the challenge. Keep stealth usage and the pinned v4.8.2 benchmark claim in the packet changelog, and prefer the agent-browser lane where stealth is not required.\"\n116:**R-SEC-3 npm binary supply chain.** \"Installation remains an operator stop-for-yes owned by 006 — never install implicitly. Pin the exact version the packet was authored against (v4.8.2) and record its read date in the packet changelog. Leave optional dependencies enabled but verify the resolved native package's SHA-256 against the published release sidecars (`shasum -a 256 -c`) before use; for higher assurance prefer the standalone prebuilt binary plus digest over npm. Re-verify CLI flags against the installed binary before relying on captured output. Roll back with `npm uninstall -g bladebro`, and remove the doctor-reported data root only after confirming no needed named sessions remain.\"\n3:description: \"Author the mcp-bladebro mode packet: CLI first with a transport-driven Code Mode MCP fallback, agent-browser default and gated real-browser lanes, R-SEC-1/2/3 safety rules, and Aside's scope unchanged.\"\n84:- **Safety rules R-SEC-1, R-SEC-2, R-SEC-3**, written into the packet verbatim as below (`research.md` §9; text from `iteration-007.md` findings 1-3).\n91:**R-SEC-1 signed-in profiles.** \"Default to the Bladebro-owned agent-browser profile; use `BLADE_HOME`/`BLADE_FRESH=1` for task isolation. Any real-browser (`rb`) lane requires an explicit operator request, and the operator must select the profile/account before control is handed over. Use `attach` whenever the browser must remain caller-owned and open; do not use `profile` on a live branded Chrome. Gate mutations behind `rb pause`/`rb resume` and keep consent-sensitive actions human-in-the-loop. Never pass `--account` to `aside mcp` or `aside repl`, and keep a single-writer lock per account/profile. Re-capture detection output each session and redact cookie/credential values.\"\n93:**R-SEC-2 stealth and site terms of service.** \"Treat stealth as operator-authorized only. Before enabling a real-browser lane on a target site, the operator must confirm the site's terms of service and access rules; do not use Bladebro to evade CAPTCHAs, anti-bot walls, or access controls where doing so breaches those terms or applicable law. A `blocked:` verdict is terminal — report it and stop; do not re-issue the action, swap fingerprints, or otherwise route around the challenge. Keep stealth usage and the pinned v4.8.2 benchmark claim in the packet changelog, and prefer the agent-browser lane where stealth is not required.\"\n95:**R-SEC-3 npm binary supply chain.** \"Installation remains an operator stop-for-yes owned by 006 — never install implicitly. Pin the exact version the packet was authored against (v4.8.2) and record its read date in the packet changelog. Leave optional dependencies enabled but verify the resolved native package's SHA-256 against the published release sidecars (`shasum -a 256 -c`) before use; for higher assurance prefer the standalone prebuilt binary plus digest over npm. Re-verify CLI flags against the installed binary before relying on captured output. Roll back with `npm uninstall -g bladebro`, and remove the doctor-reported data root only after confirming no needed named sessions remain.\"\n106:| .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md | Create | `name: mcp-bladebro`; lane rule, browser lanes, R-SEC-1/2/3, limits |\n126:| REQ-002 | Safety rules cover every KQ7 finding, verbatim | `rg -c 'R-SEC-1\\|R-SEC-2\\|R-SEC-3'` on the packet `SKILL.md` prints at least 3, and each rule's text matches section 3 |\n154:| Dependency | Upstream Bladebro releases often (about 40 in four months) | Packet goes stale | Pin v4.8.2 with its read date in the packet changelog; re-read the releases API before authoring (R-SEC-3) |\n155:| Risk | Real-browser lanes touch signed-in profiles | High | R-SEC-1: agent-browser default, explicit request plus operator-chosen profile for `rb` |\n156:| Risk | Stealth used against a site's terms | High | R-SEC-2: operator ToS gate, `blocked:` is terminal |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:46:52.843Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--rewritten-forms-rerun/results.csv rows=11 PASS=8 FAIL=2\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--signed-in-live/results.csv rows=16 PASS=10 FAIL=5\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--probe-guard-fix/results.csv rows=3 PASS=2 FAIL=0\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-11-21--two-stage-replay--compiled/results.csv rows=6 PASS=6 FAIL=0\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--clickup-real-browser/results.csv rows=6 PASS=4 FAIL=1\n\n23:- The work needs stealth on a signed-in site, and the operator has authorized it under R-SEC-2\n33:- Evading CAPTCHAs, anti-bot walls or access controls against a site's terms (R-SEC-2 forbids it)\n61:- **Neither works:** report the install command and hand the decision to the operator. Never install implicitly (R-SEC-3).\n112:**R-SEC-1 signed-in profiles.** \"Default to the Bladebro-owned agent-browser profile; use `BLADE_HOME`/`BLADE_FRESH=1` for task isolation. Any real-browser (`rb`) lane requires an explicit operator request, and the operator mus