{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JVfceKtFgjD4mShvMrkicD","type":"tool_result","content":"== .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-21--manual-testing-playbook--hub-path-live\nREADME.md\nsource.md\n3:> mcp-chrome-devtools · manual-testing-playbook · five live CLI scenarios from the mcp-browser-use hub path · bdg 0.6.10\n9:Verdict: FAIL.\n11:Five non-destructive `bdg` scenarios ran once against `<url> from the packet's new home under `mcp-browser-use`. Install, session start, the screenshot and session stop passed. The `h1` query failed: example.com served no `h1` element, so `bdg dom query \"h1\"` found no nodes.\n13:Tally: 4 PASS, 1 FAIL.\n19:| Scenario | File | Verdict | Observed |\n21:| BDG-001 | `cli-bdg-lifecycle/install-version.md` | PASS | `/opt/homebrew/bin/bdg`, version `0.6.10` |\n22:| BDG-002 | `cli-bdg-lifecycle/session-start.md` | PASS | `Session Started`, status `ACTIVE` on `<url> |\n23:| BDG-008 | `dom-and-screenshot/query-selector.md` | FAIL | `No nodes found matching \"h1\"`, grep exit 1 |\n== .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--remaining-live\nREADME.md\nsource.md\n3:> mcp-chrome-devtools · manual-testing-playbook · the 17 live scenarios no earlier run covered · bdg 0.6.10 and chrome-devtools-mcp 0.26.0\n9:Verdict: FAIL.\n11:Every live scenario the 2026-11-21 run left out ran once against `<url> Four passed as written: the CDP method search, `dom eval`, the HAR export and the cleanup-leak check. Most failures are stale scenario text, not broken tools. `bdg` 0.6.10 prints human-readable text unless it gets `--json`, so five scenarios that pipe into `jq` or grep a line format fail. Code Mode rejects the top-level `await` that all five MCP scenarios use. Three failures are real tool behavior: `bdg` ignored a bogus `CHROME_PATH`, accepted `not-a-url` as a URL and kept screenshotting after its Chrome was killed.\n13:Tally: 4 PASS, 13 FAIL.\n19:| Scenario | File | Verdict | Observed |\n21:| BDG-003 | `cli-bdg-lifecycle/status-json.md` | FAIL | `jq: parse error`, `bdg status` prints text; `bdg status --json` carries `active` and `url` |\n22:| BDG-005 | `protocol-discovery/list-cdp-domains.md` | FAIL | output is JSON with 53 domains including Page, Network and Runtime, but the line-anchored grep matched 0 lines |\n23:| BDG-006 | `protocol-discovery/describe-page-domain.md` | FAIL | `--describe Page` prints a summary (61 commands, 28 events) and names no method; `bdg cdp Page --list` does list `Page.navigate` and `Page.reload` |\n== .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/benchmark/reports/2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--routing-recall\nREADME.md\nsource.md\n3:> mcp-chrome-devtools · manual-testing-playbook · 8 intra-routing-recall scenarios · packet `ROUTER.md` replay\n9:Verdict: PASS.\n11:Every intra-routing-recall scenario in the Chrome DevTools playbook passed. Each one checks that a prompt resolves the intent and resource set its frontmatter names. This run checked the scenario contract and also replayed the prompt through the packet's own machine router. Both agreed for all 8.\n13:Tally: 8 PASS, 0 FAIL.\n19:| Scenario | File | Verdict | Observed |\n21:| CD-R05 | `intra-routing-recall/automation.md` | PASS | expected `AUTOMATION`, router chose `AUTOMATION` and loaded `references/cdp-patterns.md`, `references/session-management.md` |\n22:| CD-R01 | `intra-routing-recall/cli.md` | PASS | expected `CLI`, router chose `CLI` and loaded `references/cdp-patterns.md`, `references/session-management.md` |\n23:| CD-H02 | `intra-routing-recall/holdout-cli.md` | PASS | expected `CLI`, router chose `CLI` and loaded `references/cdp-patterns.md`, `references/session-management.md` |\n      30","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:47:08.598Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"== .skilled/