{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012E42v5irddBGNm4LuUriqC","type":"tool_result","content":"67:| `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/` | Modified | Forms corrected in nine scenarios. Root 1.0.6.0 |\n83:| `mcp-chrome-devtools/references/{session-management,troubleshooting,cdp-patterns}.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-bdg-lifecycle/session-status.md` | Modified | Every `bdg status` check uses `--json` and `.active`. Plain `bdg status` prints text, and its no-session text contains the word \"active\", so the old `grep -q \"active\"` test was always true |\n84:| `mcp-chrome-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` | Modified, 1.0.7.0 | The hand-typed census of 22 scenarios is gone; the validator derives 30 across 7 |\n97:6. The Chrome DevTools and Aside scenario forms were corrected, and both playbook roots were bumped.\n125:| `validate-playbook-package.cjs --package mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools` | Exit 0. `scenarios=30 violations=0 warnings=2` at first, both census warnings that predate this packet. `warnings=0` after the review follow-up removed the hand-typed census |\n140:1. **Rewritten Aside forms ran live afterwards.** The rerun `2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--rewritten-forms-rerun` gave 8 PASS and 2 FAIL. ASD-012 and ASD-013 failed because an early `return` in their `catch` dropped the logged line. With that fixed, `2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--probe-guard-fix` gave 2 PASS. The Chrome DevTools rewrites still have no live run, and BDG-015 stays UNKNOWN.\n142:3. **Stale old forms in consumers.** The Aside `README.md`, references and `examples/` still show `/tmp` paths or the old forms, and the Code Mode `SKILL.md` examples and CM-012 remain. The Aside `SKILL.md` and catalog rows and the Chrome DevTools `bdg status` checks were fixed in the review follow-up. The `.active` field is read from the bdg 0.6.10 source (`formatStatusAsJson`, printed unwrapped by `CommandRunner` under `--json`), not from a live run.\n147:8. **Chrome DevTools rewrites are still not live-tested.** No Chrome DevTools run folder exists. A live run of that lane needs the operator's approval.\n106:- Re-running the earlier 2026-11-22 Aside folders from 007, `app-closed-safe-set` and `routing-recall`.\n171:| Dependency | The signed-in Aside profile and the operator's ClickUp session | Without them the 15 Aside scenarios and the Bladebro real-browser scenarios cannot re-run | Each run needed an operator yes. The runs stayed read-only and recorded no page text, workspace or cookie name |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:47:15.390Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"67:| `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/` | Modified | Forms corrected in nine scenarios. Root 1.0.6.0 |\n83:| `mcp-chrome-devtools/references/{session-management,troubleshooting,cdp-patterns}.md`, `feature-catalog/cli-bdg-lifecycle/session-status.md` | Modified | Every `bdg status` check uses `--json` and `.active`. Plain `bdg status` prints text, and its no-session text contains the word \"active\", so the old `grep -q \"active\"` test was always true |\n84:| `mcp-chrome-devtools/manual-testing-playbook/manual-testing-playbook.md` | Modified, 1.0.7.0 | The hand-typed census of 22 scenarios is gone; the validator derives 30 across 7 |\n97:6. The Chrome DevTools and Aside scenario forms were corrected, and both playbook roots were bumped.\n125:| `validate-playbook-package.cjs --package mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools` | Exit 0. `scenarios=30 violations=0 warnings=2` at first, both census warnings that predate this packet. `warnings=0` after the review follow-up removed the hand-typed census |\n140:1. **Rewritten Aside forms ran live afterwards.** The rerun `2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--rewritten-forms-rerun` gave 8 PASS and 2 FAIL. ASD-012 and ASD-013 failed because an early `return` in their `catch` dropped the logged line. With that fixed, `2026-11-22--manual-testing-playbook--probe-guard-fix` gave 2 PASS. The Chrome DevTools rewrites still have no live run, and BDG-015 stays UNKNOWN.\n142:3. **Stale old forms in consumers.** The Aside `README.md`, references and `examples/` still show `/tmp` paths or the old forms, and the Code Mode `SKILL.md` examples and CM-012 remain. The Aside `SKILL.md` and catalog rows and the Chrome DevTools `bdg status` checks were fixed in the review follow-up. The `.active` field is read from the bdg 0.6.10 source (`formatStatusAsJson`, printed unwrapped by `CommandRunner` under `--json`), not from a live run.\n147:8. **Chrome DevTools rewrites are still not live-tested.** No Chrome DevTools run folder exists. A live run of that lane needs the operator's approval.\n106:- Re-running the earlier 2026-11-22 Aside folders from 007, `app-closed-safe-set` and `routing-recall`.\n171:| Dependency | The signed-in Aside profile and the operator's ClickUp session | Without them the 15 Aside scenarios and the Bladebro real-browser scenarios cannot re-run | Each run needed an operator yes. The runs stayed read-only and recorded no page text, workspace or cookie name |","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[],"moreFiles":0,"unavailable":true}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012E42v5irddBGNm4LuUriqC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
