riving without a postinstall script.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/preflight-and-install/npm-install.md:15:Plan step 3. The install runs only after the operator yes. The package runs no postinstall script, which is why installing before the digest check in BB-003 is safe.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/references/install-and-verify.md:47:| 3 | `npm install -g bladebro@4.8.2` | The package plus the native `bladebro-darwin-arm64` or `bladebro-darwin-x64` through optional dependencies; no postinstall script | `npm uninstall -g bladebro` |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/mcp-servers/bladebro-cli/README.md:35:The npm package `bladebro` is a small Node launcher. The real program is a native Rust binary that npm pulls in as an optional dependency, with no postinstall script. A standalone prebuilt binary is also published on the upstream GitHub Releases page, and with its digest it is the higher-assurance route. Installing, updating and removing Bladebro are operator decisions every time.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"<redacted>","uuid":"<redacted>","timestamp":"2026-11-24T04:49:25.486Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/doctor.sh:36:  info \"Install (operator-invoked): curl -fsSL <url> | bash\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:2:# WHY: operator-invoked wrapper around the official Aside curl installer.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:31:    3. Runs the official installer: curl -fsSL <url> | bash\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:74:command -v curl >/dev/null 2>&1 || { err \"curl not found — required to fetch the installer\"; exit 1; }\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:77:info \"curl -fsSL $INSTALLER_URL | bash\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/i