80dac4772d42a8e317e8fe099514d4db846716027000698`, generation 1 |\n---\n21:- User wants browser work that leverages a signed-in Aside account, profile sessions, or password-manager autofill\n37:- Fully unattended sensitive account actions — MFA, CAPTCHA, vault unlock, and approvals pause tasks and require a human\n83:| `aside --account <id> \"<task>\"` | Run a direct task under a selected account |\n85:| `aside account list` / `status [id]` / `use <id>` | Enumerate / inspect / select accounts |\n89:Boundary rules: `--account` is documented for direct tasks and `exec` only — never invent `aside mcp --account` or `aside repl --account`. `--session` is agent-task continuation, not an MCP browser selector. There are no typed `aside navigate/dom/screenshot/console/network` subcommands.\n95:`aside mcp` is a client-spawned local **stdio** process. It has no URL, port, token or credential field. It inherits the logged-in CLI account/provider context.\n112:1. **Agent-task continuation** — `--session <id>` continues account-scoped task state; tasks can pause for input/approval and resume.\n121:Use **one** UTCP manual and a single-writer rule per account/profile by default. The dual-manual alternative remains an unresolved open question.\nrg: --glob: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nrg: !**/benchmark/**: No such file or directory (os error 2)\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:83:| `aside --account <id> \"<task>\"` | Run a direct task under a selected account |\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:142:4. Pass `--account` to `aside mcp` or `aside repl`; it is documented for direct tasks and `exec` only.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:229:- `--version`, `--session <id>`, `--account <id>`, `--model <model>`, `--provider <provider>`\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/README.md:132:The agent-task lane covers `aside \"<task>\"`, `aside exec`, `--session <id>` continuation and `--account <id>` selection. It handles navigation, DOM inspection, screenshots, downloads and password-manager sign-in. MFA, CAPTCHA, vault unlock and approvals stay human-only.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/examples/README.md:34:./agent-task-session.sh \"Check my dashboard\" --account <id>\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/feature-catalog/task/agent-tasks.md:16:Carries goal-driven, multi-step browser work: \"sign in and download\", \"compare and book\", \"fill the form\" — jobs where the outcome matters more than the steps. The lane is the primary surface of the skill: `aside \"<task>\"` starts a natural-language browser-agent task under the signed-in account, `aside exec` adds explicit provider/model controls, `--session <id>` continues prior account-scoped task state, and `--account <id>` selects the account for a direct task.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/examples/agent-task-session.sh:13:Usage: agent-task-session.sh \"<task prompt>\" [--session <id>] [--account <id>]\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/examples/agent-task-session.sh:18:  agent-task-session.sh \"Check my dashboard\" --account <id>\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/examples/agent-task-session.sh:22:  - --account selects an account for this direct task; it is documented for\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/examples/agent-task-session.sh:35:    --account) ACCOUNT_ID=\"${2:?--account needs an id}\"; shift ;;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01RwixT4QzKCyN3C6UHT6L5v","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
