\",\"id\":1,\"method\":\"initialize\",\"params\":{\"protocolVersion\":\"2024-11-05\",\"capabilities\":{},\"clientInfo\":{\"name\":\"mcp-bladebro-doctor\",\"version\":\"1.0.0\"}}}'\nREQ_NOTE='{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"method\":\"notifications/initialized\"}'\nREQ_LIST='{\"jsonrpc\":\"2.0\",\"id\":2,\"method\":\"tools/list\",\"params\":{}}'\n\n(\n  { printf '%s\\n' \"$REQ_INIT\"; sleep 1; printf '%s\\n' \"$REQ_NOTE\" \"$REQ_LIST\"; sleep 3; } \\\n    | bladebro mcp >\"$probe_out\" 2>\"$probe_err\"\n) &\nprobe_pid=$!\nwaited=0\nwhile kill -0 \"$probe_pid\" 2>/dev/null && [ \"$waited\" -lt 30 ]; do\n  sleep 0.5\n  waited=$((waited + 1))\ndone\nkill \"$probe_pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\nwait \"$probe_pid\" 2>/dev/null || true\n\nif grep -q '\"capabilities\"' \"$probe_out\" 2>/dev/null; then","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-2/iterations/iteration-002.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":60,"lines":["+# Iteration 002 — Security: install supply chain, signed-in profile rules, teardown","+","+## Dispatcher","+- Lineage opus-2, iteration 2 (state log held 1 iteration row). steer.md absent.","+","+## Dimension","+security","+","+## Review Focus Coverage","+Checked phase 004's R-SEC-1/2/3 goal criteria and phase 007's install-script parity against the shipped scripts, the prior generation's teardown fix (R2-P1-001), and the UTCP manuals phase 004 added for the Code Mode fallback.","+","+## Files Reviewed","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:1-150`","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:112-116` (R-SEC-1/2/3)","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/manual-testing-playbook/teardown/uninstall-and-data-root.md:30-75`","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/scripts/install.sh:20-80`, `doctor.sh:36`","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/scripts/_utils.sh:837-850`, `install.sh:230`","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md:83,89,142`","+- `.utcp_config.json` (aside, bladebro, chrome_devtools_1/2/live manuals)","+","+## Findings by Severity","+","+### P0 Findings","+None.","+","+### P1 Findings","+None.","+","+### P2 Findings","+1. **Bladebro installer runs npm lifecycle scripts before the digest gate it exists to enforce** -- .skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh:111 -- `npm install -g \"bladebro@${PINNED_VERSION}\"` runs without `--ignore-scripts`, so any install or postinstall hook in the package executes before the SHA-256 check at lines 130-138. The header (lines 5-9, 18-20) says an unverifiable binary \"is the thing this wrapper exists to prevent\", and R-SEC-3 (SKILL.md:116) says to verify the resolved native package \"before use\". The check also covers only the native binary; the JS launcher at `$(npm prefix -g)/bin/bladebro`, which is what runs at line 142 and on PATH, is never compared against anything. Reach is a tampered or substituted 4.8.2 tarball on the operator's configured registry; npm version immutability and the operator stop-for-yes keep this at hardening level.","+   Finding class: supply-chain hardening gap against a stated security rule.","+   Scope proof: install.sh:111 vs install.sh:130-138 ordering; SKILL.md:116.","+   Affected surface hints: mcp-bladebro/scripts/install.sh, INSTALL-GUIDE.md install steps, R-SEC-3 wording.","+   Case: a registry-served bladebro@4.8.2 whose package.json declares a postinstall hook runs that hook during install.sh line 111 even when the later digest check fails and uninstalls the package.","+","+## Traceability Checks","+- spec_code (pass for security surfaces): R-SEC-1 \"never pass --account to aside mcp or aside repl\" is reflected in Aside SKILL.md:89 and :142 and the examples README; the teardown playbook now reads the root from `bladebro doctor`, waits for operator confirmation and asserts `root absent` (uninstall-and-data-root.md:47-52), so the prior R2-P1-001 fix holds.","+","+## Integration Evidence","+- `.utcp_config.json` manuals carry `env: {}` for aside, bladebro and the three chrome_devtools servers; no secret values. chrome-devtools-mcp is pinned at 0.26.0.","+","+## Edge Cases","+- Aside's install.sh pipes the vendor installer (`curl -fsSL <url> | bash`, line 78) with no pin or digest and honors `ASIDE_CLI_BASE_URL` from the environment. It is operator-invoked and the vendor's documented path; no goal or R-SEC rule covers Aside's install, so it is recorded here rather than as a finding.","+- `verify_command` in chrome-devtools `_utils.sh:837` uses `eval \"$cmd\"` but has no caller in the scripts folder; unreachable today.","+","+## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces","+- Bladebro install refuses non-macOS and unknown arch, never replaces an existing install, never runs `npm update`/`bladebro -u`, and uninstalls on digest mismatch.","+- R-SEC-2: `blocked:` is terminal in SKILL.md:114.","+","+## Ruled Out","+- Unconditional `rm -rf` of the Bladebro data root: fixed (playbook steps 1-6).","+- Secrets in UTCP browser manuals: none.","+","+## Next Focus","+- Dimension: traceability","+- Focus area: each phase's goal.md completion criteria against implementation-summary.md evidence and the parent spec status table; spec_code and checklist_evidence core protocols.","+- Reason: operator focus is phase goals vs shipped work; parent spec.md shows Status Complete while the phase map marks 005 Partial and the 006→007 handoff row is TBD.","+- Required evidence: goal.md criteria lines and the evidence each implementation-summary cites.","+","+Review verdict: PASS"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-2/iterations/iteration-002.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01G4fGnPWfmsx4pDD8EF2tta","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
