e router program\n1069:const HOST_SKIP_MESSAGE = \"SKIP: host repository; the authored compiled-routing source ships only in Skilled's own checkout\";\n1071:// The authored source ships only in Skilled's own checkout, so a host repository\n1072:// that vendors Skilled under `.skilled` has nothing for --check to compare. The\n  013-live-activation/activation/sk-design/manifest.json\n  013-live-activation/activation/sk-doc/manifest.json\n  013-live-activation/activation/system-deep-loop/manifest.json\n  014-runtime-engine/lib/compiled-route.cjs\n  014-runtime-engine/lib/resolve.cjs\nall 8 hubs resolve\nSYNC FAILED: 1 served file(s) out of sync; rebuild with compiled-route-sync.cjs, or copy a re-minted activation manifest back to its authored path:\n  009-parent-hub-rollout/007-sk-doc/lib/registry-compiler.cjs differs from its authored file\nexit 0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-3/iterations/iteration-004.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":0,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":75,"lines":["+# Iteration 004 — Maintainability","+","+## Dispatcher","+","+- Lineage: opus-3 (fan-out), session `fanout-opus-3-1795495435655-lf6jf3`, generation 1","+- Dimension: maintainability","+- Operator focus (every phase's shipped work against its goal criteria): this pass checked whether the last phase's shipped work (013) left the hub's version and release history in a state later phases can build on. 007's goal set up the changelog topology. 011 and 013 each claim a packet release.","+- Sources: no `steer.md` present.","+","+## Files Reviewed","+","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/SKILL.md:5`, `ROUTER.md:105-107`, `mcp-*/SKILL.md:5`","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/changelog/`, `.skilled/changelog/mcp-browser-use/` (symlink topology from 007)","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md`","+- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-aside-devtools/changelog/` (latest v1.1.12.0)","+- Commit `1a350b1512b` (013) file list for both packets","+- `specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/spec.md:126`, `013-.../spec.md:103`","+","+## Findings by Severity","+","+### P0 Findings","+","+None.","+","+### P1 Findings","+","+None.","+","+### P2 Findings","+","+1. **013 shipped script and behaviour changes in two packets without cutting a release: it rewrote 011's published v1.0.27.0 note and gave Aside no entry** -- `.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md:1` -- 013 changed 36 Chrome DevTools files, including `scripts/install.sh` (macOS Chrome detection), `scripts/_utils.sh` (Node minimum 18→20) and `scripts/doctor.sh`. It also changed 21 Aside files, including new behaviour claims in `mcp-aside-devtools/SKILL.md` on the model-flag spelling and browser-profile binding for 1.26.626.1517. The Chrome DevTools version stayed 1.0.27.0, the release the parent spec credits to 011 (`spec.md:126`), and 013 edited that existing note in place. Aside stayed at 1.1.12.0 with no new changelog file (last Aside changelog commit `3395b32f6b1`, 2026-11-22). `parent-skill-check.cjs` still passes 13d because it only compares SKILL.md with the newest entry. A reader of either changelog cannot tell that the installer's behaviour changed after 011, and the version-to-content mapping 007 set up no longer holds.","+   Finding class: release-history-drift.","+   Scope proof: `git show 1a350b1512b --stat` lists `mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/v1.0.27.0.md` as modified, not added, and no `mcp-aside-devtools/changelog/` path.","+   Affected surface hints: `mcp-chrome-devtools/changelog/`, `mcp-aside-devtools/changelog/`, both `SKILL.md` version fields, `.skilled/changelog/mcp-browser-use/` symlinks.","+   Case: an operator on Chrome DevTools 1.0.27.0 from before 013 compares versions to decide whether to re-run `install.sh`. The versions match, so they skip the Node-20 and Chrome-detection fixes.","+","+## Traceability Checks","+","+| Protocol | Status | Evidence |","+|----------|--------|----------|","+| feature_catalog_code | pass | Bladebro catalog validator reports 0 violations (iteration 3). Parent-skill-check 13d confirms all three packet versions match their newest changelog entry. |","+| skill_agent | notApplicable | The hub ships no agent definitions. Routing is skill-level through the advisor and the hub router. |","+","+## Integration Evidence","+","+- `.skilled/changelog/mcp-browser-use/parent` is a symlink to `../../skills/mcp-browser-use/changelog`, and the mode folders mirror the packet changelogs, so 007's topology is one source of truth and not a duplicate.","+- `ROUTER.md:107` now states that `mcp-browser-use` serves compiled routing by default. `compiled-route.cjs:38` registers the hub. 005's \"legacy sentinel\" verification row is historical, and the live state has moved past it, with the advisor returning `compiledRoute.action: route` (iteration 1).","+","+## Edge Cases","+","+- The duplicated `_utils.sh` helper is a deliberate per-skill copy guarded by a lockstep test. Its drift is already R1-P1-001 and is not re-raised here.","+- 005's implementation summary still describes stage two as legacy-served. It is a dated record of that phase, and its claim was superseded rather than wrong at the time, so it is not a finding.","+","+## Confirmed-Clean Surfaces","+","+- Hub version 1.1.1.0 is consistent across SKILL.md, the JSON routing files and the newest hub changelog (parent-skill-check 13a/13b).","+- The changelog topology from 007 resolves through symlinks with no dangling link in the listed folders.","+","+## Ruled Out","+","+- Duplicate changelog trees: the `.skilled/changelog/mcp-browser-use/*` entries are symlinks.","+","+## Next Focus","+","+- Dimension: correctness (stabilization)","+- Focus area: replay the two active P1s against the current files (`_utils.sh` diff, Bladebro SKILL.md:60). Check parent goal criterion 7 and the 001-research criterion (≥10 iteration records, research.md exists), which no pass has run yet.","+- Reason: all four dimensions are covered. A stabilization pass confirms the active P1s and closes the remaining parent criterion.","+- Rotation status: all canonical dimensions covered once.","+- Required evidence: file:line rereads.","+","+## Verdict","+","+No new P0/P1 this iteration. Two P1 findings from iterations 1 and 2 remain active, so the verdict over active findings is CONDITIONAL.","+","+Review verdict: CONDITIONAL"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-3/iterations/iteration-004.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_0138S589zFsk2NriG7QaziLL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
