{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SCGewggJyp9CQqk4vTP7qB","type":"tool_result","content":".skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-24-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md:25:Call the tools through `call_tool_chain()` with the manual namespace, for example `chrome_devtools_1.chrome_devtools_1_lighthouse_audit({ ... })`. Confirm each name with `list_tools()` or `tool_info()` before the first call, because the exposed tool set changes between releases and this leaf freezes no count.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-26-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-27-- **Lighthouse audit.** Open the page with `new_page`, run `lighthouse_audit`, then read the scores and the flagged nodes. Read the saved report for the full audit list.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-28-- **Performance trace.** Start `performance_start_trace`, load or interact with the page, stop with `performance_stop_trace`, then pass a named insight from the result to `performance_analyze_insight`.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-29-- **Cleanup.** Close the pages the program opened in a `finally` block, as the session-cleanup leaf describes.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-30-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-31----\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-32-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-chrome-devtools/feature-catalog/mcp-parallel-instances/lighthouse-and-performance-trace.md-33-## 3. SOURCE FILES\n--\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-3-description: \"Bladebro browser driver: CLI first, MCP via Code Mode as fallback; owned agent-browser default, gated real-browser lanes.\"\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:4:allowed-tools: [Read, Write, Edit, Bash, Glob, Grep, mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain]\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-5-version: 1.2.0.0\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-6----\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-7-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-8-# Bladebro Browser Driver - CLI + MCP Integration\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-9-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-10-Agentic browser work through Bladebro: five tools (`act`, `see`, `state`, `run`, `vision`) behind one Rust binary. The CLI and the `bladebro mcp` stdio server share the same handlers, so this packet picks a transport, then a browser lane, then checks the safety rules before any action.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-11-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-12-Every Bladebro fact here is upstream documentation pinned to v4.8.2 and read 2026-11-21. The install and the agent-browser lane ran live on macOS arm64 on 2026-11-21. The real-browser `clone` reads failed there, and the results are in `benchmark/reports/`.\n--\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-68-    +- binary present, doctor passes, standalone work  -> bladebro CLI\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:69:    +- binary missing, or composition / parallel / MCP-only -> bladebro manual via call_tool_chain()\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-70-    +- neither available                               -> operator install decision (no install here)\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-71-```\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-72-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-73-### Browser Lanes\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-74-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-75-The owned agent-browser profile is the default lane. It needs no request and touches no personal profile. Use `BLADE_HOME` or `BLADE_FRESH=1` to isolate a task.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-76-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-77-The real-browser `rb` lanes (`auto`, `clone`, `profile`, `attach`, plus `pause`/`resume`, `off`, `forget`) run only on an explicit operator request:\n--\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-159-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md:160:Use Bash for the `bladebro` CLI, Read for references, and Glob for saved images and artifacts. Use `mcp__code_mode__call_tool_chain` only after a Code Mode session has loaded the `bladebro` manual and `search_tools()` or `tool_info()` confirmed its callables.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-161-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-162-### Sibling Packets\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-163-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-164-`mcp-chrome-devtools` owns CDP-level debugging and its captures. `mcp-aside-devtools` owns deterministic signed-in proof. `mcp-code-mode` owns the MCP transport.\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-165-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-166----\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-167-\n.skilled/skills/mcp-browser-use/mcp-bladebro/SKILL.md-168-## 7. QUICK REFERENCE","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id"