location/acceptance-criteria.md:94` | AC-002 row is Met (`:60`) and the rg pair prints nothing on the current tree (iteration 1). The closure anchor still says \"Closeable: No / AC-002 is unmet\" (`:92-94`). goal.md logs \"Criterion 2 Unmet\" (`:87`) with all five criteria unchecked (`:58-62`). implementation-summary.md keeps completion_pct 90 and next_safe_action \"Await operator choice on AC-002\" (`:14,35`). A resume of 003 would reopen finished work. AC_CLOSURE reads only the rows, so validation passes; only the prose is stale | Set the closure statement to Yes, check the goal criteria with evidence, and update the continuity | packet-doc state drift / 003 docs only / closure anchor, goal, summary |","+| O4-I3-P2-002 | P2 | traceability | `004-bladebro-mode/goal.md:21` | All five criteria are unchecked and continuity reads \"Authored the durable directive\", completion_pct 0. Every criterion holds (iteration 1), and the parent binds this goal as authoritative | Check the criteria with evidence and refresh the continuity | packet-doc state drift / 004 goal.md / completion anchor, continuity |","+| O4-I3-P2-003 | P2 | traceability | `spec.md:146` | The 006 to 007 handoff row still reads \"[Criteria TBD] / [Verification TBD]\" in a packet marked Complete | Name the criterion and its verification command | template residue / one row / handoff table |","+| O4-I3-P2-004 | P2 | traceability | `spec.md:17` | Parent spec.md and goal.md continuity: last_updated 2026-11-21T12:30Z, completion_pct 0, next_safe_action \"Start 002-hub-scaffold\" (`spec.md:14-24`, `goal.md:14-24`), while the status says Complete | Refresh both continuity blocks | continuity drift / parent frontmatter / spec.md, goal.md |","+| O4-I4-P2-001 | P2 | maintainability | `mcp-aside-devtools/examples/repl-evidence-capture.sh:12` | The default `OUT_DIR=/tmp/aside-evidence` is the form the example's own README (`examples/README.md:51`) says fails on Aside 1.26.626.1517. The playbook's ASD-007 already uses `./tmp/` plus in-REPL `fs` checks and passed live. A no-argument run fails its own artifact check | Adopt the ASD-007 form in the script and the README | stale example after a verified fix / one script + README row |","+","+## 4. Remediation Workstreams","+","+1. P0: none. P1: none.","+2. WS1, gate-clearing (P2, needed for the coverage gate): O4-I3-P2-001, then O4-I3-P2-002.","+3. WS2, parent hygiene (P2 advisories): O4-I3-P2-003, O4-I3-P2-004.","+4. WS3, example (P2 advisory): O4-I4-P2-001.","+","+## 5. Spec Seed","+","+- 003: the closure statement, goal criteria and continuity record AC-002 as met. cite-drift-redirects.json already carries the moved path.","+- 004: the goal criteria record the evidence that 004's own implementation summary and iteration 1 of this review hold.","+- Parent: a real 006 to 007 handoff gate (for example, the 007 goal's guard and changelog checks), and continuity set at program completion.","+","+## 6. Plan Seed","+","+- T1: Edit the 003 closure anchor, goal completion and log, and implementation-summary continuity.","+- T2: Edit the 004 goal completion anchor and continuity.","+- T3: Edit parent spec.md:146 and both parent continuity blocks.","+- T4: Switch repl-evidence-capture.sh to the ASD-007 path form and update README 2.2.","+- T5: Run `validate.sh --strict --recursive` on the packet, then re-review checklist_evidence.","+","+## 7. Traceability Status","+","+### Core Protocols","+| Protocol | Gate | Final status | Iterations | Notes |","+|----------|------|--------------|------------|-------|","+| `spec_code` | hard | pass | 1-7 | Goal criteria re-run as written; R-SEC text matches the 004 spec verbatim; versions match their changelogs |","+| `checklist_evidence` | hard | partial | 3, 5, 6, 7 | The 003 closure, goal and continuity and the 004 goal disagree with the shipped tree (O4-I3-P2-001/002). Tasks are open only where documented (004 manual check deferred to 006; 005 T020/T021 blocked with not-met notes) |","+","+### Overlay Protocols","+| Protocol | Status | Notes |","+|----------|--------|-------|","+| `skill_agent` | pass | The hub SKILL.md mode table names the three registry modes |","+| `feature_catalog_code` | pass | Chrome catalog totals 31 with the Lighthouse leaf linked; the leaf defers tool names to list_tools/tool_info |","+| `playbook_capability` | pass | Scenario files: Chrome 30, Aside 29, Bladebro 15, matching the 007/008 goals |","+| `agent_cross_runtime` | notApplicable | No agent definition is in scope |","+","+AC_COVERAGE: 003, 007 and 008 are Level 2 with acceptance-criteria.md. This review did not run the advisory rule because it writes outside the lineage. 003's rows are all Met.","+","+## 8. Deferred Items","+","+- Not independently re-run, because they write outside the lineage: stage-one advisor replay (parent criterion 5, 005 criterion 1, 013 criterion 1) and `validate.sh --strict --recursive` (parent criterion 7 and several children). Recorded evidence was relied on.","+- 012's alignment evidence lives in a private, git-ignored location by design. It exists on this host but cannot be re-checked elsewhere.","+- Seen and not re-raised, because the prior generation deferred them to the operator: C2-I1-P2-001 (bare `aside` substring makes \"Aside from that, run lighthouse\" an ordered bundle; still reproducible), C2-I2-P2-003 (`auto` rb lane attaches to any reachable endpoint), R2-P2-003 (Chrome `sudo npm` hint).","+- The Bladebro digest constants are duplicated in install.sh and doctor.sh. They agree today; consolidate if a third copy appears.","+- No frontier object in the registry: default depth mode.","+","+## Dimension Expansion Map","+","+- Saturated directions: none recorded by the reducer. Pivots: 0 completed, 0 failed, 0 audited overrides.","+- Recovery passes: iteration 3 (traceability protocol replay) and iteration 7 (severity escalation), both after a STUCK_RECOVERY decision.","+- Remaining frontier: none.","+","+## 9. Search Ledger","+","+*No search-depth state captured (legacy v1 record)*. The iteration records are unversioned and carry no searchLedger. Ruled-out directions are listed per iteration and in the Audit Appendix. hasSearchDebt: false.","+","+## 10. Audit Appendix","+","+- Convergence: 7 iterations, stop reason `maxIterationsReached`, blockedBy `dimensionCoverageGate`. New-findings ratios by iteration: 0, 0, 1.0, 0.2, 0, 0, 0. convergence.cjs returned STUCK_RECOVERY before iterations 3 and 7, and CONTINUE before 4, 5 and 6. Terminal gates: evidence pass, scope pass, coverage fail (`traceability-incomplete`).","+- Coverage: all four dimensions covered (correctness 1, 5; security 2; traceability 3, 5, 6, 7; maintainability 4, 7).","+- Ruled out: drift between the compiled-routing bundle and its copy (byte-identical); top-level await in Code Mode examples (the hits are Aside REPL snippets); teardown `rm -rf` on an arbitrary root (operator confirmation comes first); `eval` in Chrome `_utils.sh` (internal literals only); parent Complete against 005 Partial (the status line names the unmet requirements); stale stage-one tool (skill_advisor.py exists); dangling changelog links (none); P1 upgrade of the 003 closure drift (AC_CLOSURE reads rows that are Met).","+- Sources: the parent and 13 child goal/spec/tasks/acceptance-criteria/implementation-summary docs; hub and mode registries; `compiled-route.cjs` (live replay of 6 prompts); the compiled-routing router and authored bundle; mutation manifest, pre-commit hook and guard; Bladebro, Aside and Chrome scripts, examples, references and playbooks; benchmark run folders; sk-code ROUTER.md:193; `compiled-route-sync.cjs --check`; `.skilled/changelog/mcp-browser-use/`; the system-spec-kit AC_CLOSURE contract.","+- Fan-out: `step_fanout_merge` was skipped because this lineage config has no `fanout` key. The root merge owns cross-lineage results.","+- Process deviations, disclosed:","+  - No convergence pass ran before iterations 1-2.","+  - The coverage graph (`graph-db/`, inside the lineage) was seeded after iteration 2.","+  - Iteration 3's recovery_started row precedes its graph_convergence_evaluated row: the first graph payload was refused for its shape and re-sent after the fix.","+  - A `sed -i ''` edit ran on the lineage's own helper `prompts/convev.cjs`. It is listed as a scope note in iteration 7. No file outside the lineage was modified.","+  - `step_stage_artifact_dir` (git add) and `phase_save` (generate-context.js) were skipped under the lineage write limits.","+","+Review verdict: FAIL"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Skilled/specs/mcp/mcp-browser-use/001-mcp-browser-use-hub/review/lineages/opus-4/review-report.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013Qren34L2wxgYRUcpK87Rv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
